---
description: Chunking fixture builders contract for RagDataTools tests
globs:
  - RagDataTools.UnitTests/TestData/**/*.cs
  - RagDataTools.UnitTests/Chunkers/TestData/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

When you add or extend a chunking fixture builder, keep the test data reusable and stable.

## 1) Keep fluent chaining with the derived builder type

If a builder exposes a derived fluent API, keep returning the concrete builder type so tests can chain scenario setup.

## 2) Cover the chunking fixture families

Provide reusable fixture builders/helpers for these data shapes:

1. Code blocks
2. Tables
3. Images
4. Info blocks
5. Strange-word / odd-markup text
6. Topics / headings
7. Code block count ranges

Prefer explicit builder parameters over hard-coded single scenarios when a test needs variation.

## 3) Keep fixture output canonical

- Build markdown and chunk inputs from the same reusable helpers.
- Keep fixture data focused on content shape, not on strategy implementation details.
- Avoid mixing unrelated chunking concerns into one helper unless the test data is intentionally mixed.

